Now C must satisfy:
- |C| = 3
- |A∩C| = 1: C contains exactly one element from {a₁, a₂, a₃}
- |B∩C| = 1: C contains exactly one element from {a₁, b₁, b₂}

For Case 1: C = {a₁, d₃, d₄}
- |A∩C| = |{a₁, a₂, a₃} ∩ {a₁, d₃, d₄}| = |{a₁}| = 1 ✓
- |B∩C| = |{a₁, d₁, d₂} ∩ {a₁, d₃, d₄}| = |{a₁}| = 1 ✓

For Case 2: C = {a₂, d₁, d₃}
- |A∩C| = |{a₁, a₂, a₃} ∩ {a₂, d₁, d₃}| = |{a₂}| = 1 ✓
- |B∩C| = |{a₁, d₁, d₂} ∩ {a₂, d₁, d₃}| = |{d₁}| = 1 ✓
